!     PRIOR TO ITS USE IN THE CALCULATIONS, THIS FILE HAS TO BE MODIFIED.
!     DEPENDING ON WHAT BATH GAS (DILUTANT) IS MOST ABUNDANT IN YOUR SYSTEM
!     (THE PRESENT CHOICES ARE N2, AR, OR HE),  YOU  SHOULD UNCOMMENT THE
!     CORRESPONDING BLOCK FOR THE REACTION H+O2(+M)=HO2(+M), AND COMMENT THE
!     BLOCK FOR OTHER DILUTANT(S).  AS GIVEN, THE MAIN DILUTANT IS SET TO BE N2.
!     SHIELD THE LOW-TEMPERATURE SPECIES AND THEIR RELATED REACTIONS WHEN PERFORM A FLAME SIMULATION.

ELEMENTS
C H N AR HE O
END

SPECIES

!
!C0
 AR        N2          H          H2         HE
 O         OH          H2O        HO2        H2O2       O2                                    

!C1                                                     
 C         CH          CH2        CH2*       CH3        CH4       
 CO        CO2         CH2O       HCO        CH2OH      CH3O     
 CH3OH     HOCHO       HOCH2O     HCOH
 HOCO      OCHO        !HCOO

!C2                                                     
 C2H       C2H2        H2CC       C2H3       C2H4       C2H5      C2H6        
 C2O       HCCO        CH2CO      CH3CO      CH3CHO     C2H3OH    C2H5O     
 CH2OCH    CH2OCH2     CH2CHO     HCCOH      C2H4OH     HCCHOH    CH2COH    
 SC2H4OH   C2H5OH      O2CH2CHO   HO2CH2CO   CH3CO2 
 CH2CHOO   
 

!C3                                                     
 C3H3     C2H3CHO    C2H5CHO    CH3CHCO     C2H5CO     C2H3CO                 

!#####LT SPECIES######!

!ADD species for CH4
CH3O2     CH3O2H    CH2O2H

!ADD species for CH3CHO
CH3CO3     CH3CO3H      OCOCHO    KHO2COCHO   O2QCH2CO3H    QCH2CO3H
H2COCO#    CH2CO2
CH2CO2H    CH3CO2H

END


